**13. LIABILITY AND INDEMNITY**

13.1 Subject to Clause 13.2, the Contractor shall be liable for and shall indemnify the Client against any loss, damage, cost, expense, claim, demand, or proceeding arising out of or in connection with:

(a) any breach of this Agreement by the Contractor;

(b) any negligence, fraud, or wilful misconduct on the part of the Contractor, its personnel, subcontractors, or agents in the performance of the Works;

(c) any infringement of any patent, trademark, copyright, or other intellectual property right arising from the performance of the Works or the use by the Client of any deliverable produced under this Agreement;

(d) any injury to or death of any person, or loss of or damage to any property, caused by the acts or omissions of the Contractor, its personnel, subcontractors, or agents, except to the extent that such injury, death, loss, or damage is caused by the negligence or breach of this Agreement by the Client.

13.2 The Contractor's aggregate liability under or in connection with this Agreement, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty, or otherwise, shall not exceed the total contract value stated in Clause 12.1, except that this limitation shall not apply to:

(a) liability for death or personal injury caused by the Contractor's negligence;

(b) liability for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation;

(c) liability arising under Clause 13.1(c) (intellectual property infringement);

(d) liability arising under Clause 16 (Confidentiality); or

(e) any other liability that cannot be limited or excluded under applicable law.

13.3 The Contractor shall maintain, at its own cost, comprehensive insurance coverage with reputable insurers duly licensed by the National Insurance Commission of Nigeria, for the duration of this Agreement and for a period of twelve (12) months thereafter, as follows:

(a) Employer's Liability and Workmen's Compensation insurance in accordance with the Employees' Compensation Act, 2010, with a limit of not less than Fifty Million Naira (NGN 50,000,000) per occurrence;

(b) Public Liability insurance with a limit of not less than One Hundred Million Naira (NGN 100,000,000) per occurrence;

(c) Professional Indemnity insurance with a limit of not less than One Hundred Million Naira (NGN 100,000,000) per claim, covering the professional services rendered under this Agreement;

(d) All Risks insurance covering the Contractor's equipment, tools, and temporary works brought to the Site, with a limit of not less than the replacement value of such equipment, tools, and temporary works; and

(e) Motor Vehicle insurance covering all vehicles used in connection with the Works, with a limit of not less than Fifty Million Naira (NGN 50,000,000) per occurrence.

13.4 The Contractor shall, upon the Client's reasonable request, provide certificates of insurance and evidence of payment of premiums for all insurance policies required under Clause 13.3. The Client shall have the right to review the adequacy of such insurance coverage and to require the Contractor to increase the limits of coverage where, in the Client's reasonable opinion, the risks associated with the Works so warrant.

13.5 The insurance policies referred to in Clause 13.3 shall name the Client as an additional insured, to the extent of the Contractor's liabilities under this Agreement, and shall include a waiver of subrogation in favour of the Client.

